From cb8261336d6e431d4669c5d32a0a883d77a54281 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:57:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 606/638] Add a drawer icon for the Chromium drawer

SYS:Applications/Internet/Chromium had no .info of its own. Wanderer only
shows an object that has one, so the drawer was invisible from Workbench and
the tool icon inside it could not be reached at all - the browser was
installed with no way to get to it short of a shell.

TYPE = DRAWER, sharing Chromium.png so the drawer is branded rather than a
generic folder. No tooltypes and no STACK: those belong on the tool icon.
---
 chrome/app/theme/aros/ChromiumDrawer.info.src | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 chrome/app/theme/aros/ChromiumDrawer.info.src

diff --git a/chrome/app/theme/aros/ChromiumDrawer.info.src b/chrome/app/theme/aros/ChromiumDrawer.info.src
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..c64e20aafb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/chrome/app/theme/aros/ChromiumDrawer.info.src
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+; Drawer icon for SYS:Applications/Internet/Chromium.
+;
+; Distinct from Chromium.info.src, which is the TOOL icon for the executable
+; *inside* this drawer. Wanderer only shows an object that has its own .info,
+; so without this the Chromium drawer is invisible from Workbench and the
+; program icon inside it cannot be reached at all - the browser is installed
+; and there is no way to get to it without a shell.
+;
+; No tooltypes and no STACK here: those belong to the tool icon. A drawer icon
+; carries only its appearance and the window geometry Wanderer opens it with.
+TYPE = DRAWER
